commit 0e62c26ba4a0bb2d90569421a7bf7f9f8990d165

C03: Spanish click verbs reach input.visible.click; surface change verifies a stateless control; digit aliases; reviewed click turns (UI1273 repair)

«apretá el 5», «pulsá el 7», «presioná el nueve», «hacé clic en el botón
nueve» and «en la calculadora apretá el 5» resolved to nothing: the
pointing vocabulary and the direct-request heads lacked the Spanish forms
and the app context was read as label. A UIA-invoked control that stays
enabled and unselected (a Calculator digit) reported
visible_button_postread_unchanged; the adapter now compares the foreground
surface before and after the script and accepts a changed surface, as the
descriptor already allowed. Digit labels match their spoken names in UI
Automation («Cinco»). The reviewed turn admits input.visible.click under
root approval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


